# The R36S's OTG port as a USB host for good (package/usbrole). usbrole
# makes a port a host only while the USB PHY's ID pin (its extcon's
# USB-HOST cable) asks for power, and on the R36S nothing can: the PHY's
# otg-port, which reads that pin, is disabled in ROCKNIX's R36S tree
# (rk3326-gameconsole-r3xs.dtsi, &u2phy) and in the R36S's stock trees
# (dArkOSen-R36S's boot/dtb/r36s/*/rk3326-r36s-linux.dtb, at
# djparentx/dArkOSen-R36S 28f5427f7ae953ee6e813618705baf569fef0f27), so
# usbrole kept the port a device and nothing plugged in it worked (Sylver,
# 2026-11-27). The stock firmware leaves the controller's dr_mode "otg"
# with no way to detect a role, which makes it a host
# (KERNEL/USB_Gadget_Mass_Storage.md there), and px30.dtsi's role switch
# starts it as one. Its DC port charges; this one powers what is plugged
# in (the device tree's vbus-supply, the RK817's OTG_SWITCH).
ROLE=host
